    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d718">

                <pb facs="0946" n="850" xml:id="pg850"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Moulton to Mr.
                            Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Demerara, British Guiana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1898-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4,
                                1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform the Department
                    that in obedience to superior authority a proclamation<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d718-f1"/> of neutrality to be observed between Spain and the United
                    States has been issued and published in British Guiana and Dutch Guiana.</p>
                <p>I inclose the proclamation as published in British Guiana.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George H. Moulton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d718-f1" n="1" xml:id="d718-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. The proclamation, after the formal preamble, quotes the terms of the
                    act in regard to the conduct of British subjects and of the rules governing
                    ships of belligerents given in the proclamation of neutrality of Great Britain,
                    see <ref target="#pg865">p. 865</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
